---
export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [
    {
      slug: "controller",
      name: "Origin89 Controller",
      kicker: "Hardware & firmware / In development",
      heading: "Control stays\nwith your site.",
      intro:
        "Connect equipment from across the site and give configured rules a local place to run. The Controller is the hardware foundation of Origin89.",
      visual: "controller",
      features: [
        [
          "A place for mixed equipment.",
          "Integration work starts with the exact model, its interface and the readings or actions you need. Solar, storage, backup power and local sensors can be considered as parts of the same site.",
        ],
        [
          "A local control architecture.",
          "Configured decisions run on the Controller. The app is a client of the site, so opening a phone screen is separate from running a control rule.",
        ],
        [
          "An open hardware direction.",
          "Editable electronics and enclosure designs are part of the project. Public design packages and hardware licensing belong alongside the firmware release.",
        ],
      ],
    },
    {
      slug: "offgrid",
      name: "Origin89 Offgrid",
      kicker: "Your site app / Interface concept",
      heading: "The readings you need.\nIn one place.",
      intro:
        "Bring battery reserve, generation, temperature and equipment status into a view that makes sense for your site. See the latest received data and how old it is.",
      visual: "app",
      features: [
        [
          "Start with your site’s priorities.",
          "A cottage owner might check battery reserve and inside temperature. A maple operation might start with a tank and pump. The view should follow the equipment and questions that matter to you.",
        ],
        [
          "Keep freshness visible.",
          "A reading includes when it was received. If a connection drops, the view keeps the age visible and stops describing the data as current. Missing values remain unknown.",
        ],
        [
          "Manage the setup you have.",
          "Bring supported equipment readings and settings into one app. The open-source direction includes the app and the interfaces needed to adapt it over time.",
        ],
      ],
    },
    {
      slug: "buddy",
      name: "Origin89 Buddy",
      kicker: "Your assistant in the app & docs / Concept",
      heading: "Understand what\nyour site is telling you.",
      intro:
        "Buddy helps explain a reading, find equipment context and work through a proposed setting. Useful help starts with the actual site and the data available.",
      visual: "buddy",
      features: [
        [
          "Explain a reading in context.",
          "A battery percentage becomes more useful when you can see its source and age. Buddy should help you understand what is known and what still needs checking.",
        ],
        [
          "Prepare a change you can review.",
          "The assistant can help describe a proposed change and its purpose. The interface keeps that proposal separate from a confirmed action.",
        ],
        [
          "Keep control decisions explicit.",
          "Buddy is an assistant in the app and documentation. Deterministic control belongs to the Controller, with defined rules and equipment boundaries.",
        ],
      ],
    },
    {
      slug: "cottages",
      name: "Cottages & remote homes",
      kicker: "Your site / Cottages & off-grid homes",
      heading: "Built over years.\nManaged together.",
      intro:
        "A panel kit one summer. A different inverter the next. A generator when you need backup. Origin89 starts with the setup you could afford and the equipment worth keeping.",
      visual: "site",
      features: [
        [
          "Begin with a useful view.",
          "Battery reserve, solar generation and inside temperature are a practical starting point. Choose what you need to check before the next trip.",
        ],
        [
          "Add equipment over time.",
          "A pump, a tank sensor or a larger bank should enter an exact-model integration discussion. Find existing research before choosing the next piece of equipment.",
        ],
        [
          "Plan for the connection you have.",
          "Local control is part of the architecture. Remote viewing requires connectivity, and a disconnected app must show the age of its last received readings.",
        ],
      ],
    },
    {
      slug: "maple",
      name: "Maple operations",
      kicker: "Your site / Maple operations",
      heading: "See the equipment\nbehind the season.",
      intro:
        "Pumps, tanks, temperature probes and remote power each tell part of the story. Plan an Origin89 setup around the readings your operation needs.",
      visual: "site",
      features: [
        [
          "Put the process in context.",
          "Start with the pump status, tank level or temperature that matters to your work. Define which reading is needed and where it comes from.",
        ],
        [
          "Work with the existing installation.",
          "List the actual probes, drives, pumps and interfaces. The catalogue helps identify research and gaps before an integration is promised.",
        ],
        [
          "Keep local decisions at the equipment.",
          "Configured control rules belong at the site. Monitoring, electrical control and installation requirements need to be scoped for the operation.",
        ],
      ],
    },
    {
      slug: "field",
      name: "Remote field & industrial sites",
      kicker: "Your site / Field & industrial equipment",
      heading: "A clearer view\nof remote equipment.",
      intro:
        "Plan local monitoring and control for pumps, tanks, environmental sensors and the power systems around them. Start with a specific equipment task.",
      visual: "site",
      features: [
        [
          "Start with a defined job.",
          "Identify the measurement or supported action you need, the model involved and the connection available. This gives an integration a concrete scope.",
        ],
        [
          "Connect the interface to the outcome.",
          "The research spans communication protocols and local I/O. A documented interface is a starting point for engineering and hardware validation.",
        ],
        [
          "Make maintenance understandable.",
          "Local rules, readable status and the open-stack direction give installers a way to reason about a setup as it changes. Product suitability remains installation-specific.",
        ],
      ],
    },
  ].map((page) => ({ params: { detail: page.slug }, props: { page } }));
}
const { page } = Astro.props;
---
<Shell title={page.name}>
<section class="frame product-page-hero"><div><span class="micro">{page.kicker}</span><h1>{page.heading.split('\n').map((line:string,i:number)=><>{i>0&&<br/>}{line}</>)}</h1><p>{page.intro}</p><div class="actions"><a class="action" href={page.visual==='app'?'/next/sample-site/':'/next/plan/'}>{page.visual==='app'?'Explore a sample site':'Plan your setup'} <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-action" href="/next/equipment/">Find your equipment ↗</a></div></div>
<div class="product-page-visual">
{page.visual==='controller'&&<img src={art.controller} alt="CAD concept of the Origin89 Controller" />}
{page.visual==='buddy'&&<img src={art.buddy} alt="Buddy explaining an idea" />}
{(page.visual==='app'||page.visual==='site')&&<div class="product-art app-art"><div><span>{page.slug==='maple'?'MAPLE OPERATION':page.slug==='field'?'FIELD STATION':'NORTH COTTAGE'}</span><b>Site overview</b><strong>{page.slug==='maple'?'62':page.slug==='field'?'84':'78'}<small>%</small></strong><span>{page.slug==='maple'?'Tank level':'Battery reserve'} · Sample data</span><hr/><span>Connection <b>Local</b></span><span>Data <b>Illustrative</b></span></div></div>}
</div></section>
<section class="frame page-body"><div class="feature-rows">{page.features.map(([heading,body]:string[])=><article><h3>{heading}</h3><p>{body}</p></article>)}</div>{page.visual==='app'&&<section class="subsection"><span class="micro">Explore the proposed experience</span><h2>What a connection change looks like.</h2><Console interactive /></section>}{page.visual==='controller'&&<p class="small-note">Existing CAD render, retaining earlier enclosure artwork. Hardware is in development; this is not a shipping product photograph.</p>}<div class="actions"><a class="text-action" href="/next/system/">Compare the product roles ↗</a><a class="text-action" href="/next/open/">Explore the open stack ↗</a></div></section><CTA />
</Shell>
